'''4.''' Having the power to produce or support growth in plants: as, the ''vegetative'' properties of soil.—{{smaller|'''Vegetative reproduction,''' a form of reproduction in plants by means of cells which are not specially modified for the purpose, but which form a part of the body of the individual. Propagation by cuttings, by means of buds, soredia, gemmæ, bulbils, etc., are familiar examples. See ''reproduction,'' 3 (''a'').}}

