'''vegetativeness''' (vej′ẹ̄-tā-tiv-nes), ''n.'' The character of being vegetative, in any sense.

'''vegete''' (vej′ēt), ''a.'' [= Pg. It. ''vegeto'', < L. ''vegetus'', vigorous, brisk: see ''vegetable'', ''vegetate''.] Vigorous; active. [Rare.]
{{smaller block|He [Lucius Cornelius] had lived a healthful and ''vegete'' age till his last sickness. ''Jer. Taylor'', Holy Dying, iv. 1.}}
{{smaller block|But would my picture be complete if I forgot that ample and ''vegete'' countenance of Mr. R—— of W.?
{{right|''Lowell'', Study Windows, p. 380.}}}}

